usage: gossamer download [-h] -o OUTPUT_PATH [--min-bytes MIN_BYTES]
                         [--max-bytes MAX_BYTES] [--expect-format {auto,pdf}]
                         [--overwrite] [--try-mirrors URL [URL ...]]
                         [--resume] [--cache-dir CACHE_DIR] [--config CONFIG]
                         [--keystore KEYSTORE] [--log-level LOG_LEVEL]
                         [--fetch-mode {auto,browser,static}]
                         source

positional arguments:
  source                Remote HTTP(S) URL

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -o, --output OUTPUT_PATH
                        Destination file path
  --min-bytes MIN_BYTES
  --max-bytes MAX_BYTES
                        Maximum bytes (0 uses configured max_response_bytes)
  --expect-format {auto,pdf}
                        Validate PDF magic when set to pdf (auto infers from
                        .pdf output)
  --overwrite           Replace an existing destination
  --try-mirrors URL [URL ...]
                        Try caller-supplied alternate URLs sequentially after
                        the primary URL fails
  --resume              Continue an existing partial file with Range/If-Range
                        when the server supports it
  --cache-dir CACHE_DIR
                        Cache directory (default: ./.gossamer_cache)
  --config CONFIG       Explicit gossamer.json path
  --keystore KEYSTORE   Explicit keys.json path
  --log-level LOG_LEVEL
                        DEBUG/INFO/WARNING/ERROR (default WARNING)
  --fetch-mode {auto,browser,static}
                        Baseline render strategy for page fetches: auto
                        (default), browser, or static (env GOSSAMER_FETCH_MODE
                        / gossamer.json fetch_mode)
